<title>SPAIN: SOCCER-RESULTS/STANDINGS IN THE SPANISH LEAGUE.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-RESULTS/STANDINGS IN THE SPANISH LEAGUE.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the Spanish league</p>
<p>championship on Sunday:</p>
<p> Celta Vigo	  4   Real Madrid     0</p>
<p> Deportivo Coruna  1   Extremadura     0</p>
<p> Hercules	    3   Athletic Bilbao 2</p>
<p> Rayo Vallecano    1   Barcelona	 2</p>
<p> Oviedo		0   Sporting Gijon  0</p>
<p> Racing Santander  1   Sevilla	   4</p>
<p> Real Sociedad     2   Logrones	  1</p>
<p> Zaragoza	    1   Compostela	3</p>
<p>played Saturday:</p>
<p> Real Betis	  2   Valladolid	0</p>
<p> Espanyol	    3   Valencia	  2</p>
<p>playing Monday:</p>
<p> Atletico Madrid  v    Tenerife</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>				   P   W   D   L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> 1.Real Madrid		42  27  11   4  85   36   92</p>
<p> 2.Barcelona		  42  28   6   8 102   48   90</p>
<p> 3.Deportivo Coruna	 42  21  14   6  56   30   77</p>
<p> 4.Real Betis		 42  21  14   7  81   46   77</p>
<p> 5.Atletico Madrid	  41  20  11  10  76   63   71</p>
<p> 6.Athletic Bilbao	  42  16  16  10  72   57   67</p>
<p> 7.Valladolid		 42  18  10  14  57   46   64</p>
<p> 8.Real Sociedad	    42  18   9  15  49   46   63</p>
<p> 9.Valencia		   42  15  11  16  63   59   56</p>
<p> 10.Tenerife		  41  14  11  16  64   55   53</p>
<p> 11.Compostela		42  13  14  15  52   65   53</p>
<p> 12.Espanyol		  42  14   9  19  51   57   51</p>
<p> 13.Racing Santander	42  11  17  14  52   54   50</p>
<p> 14.Zaragoza		  42  12  14  16  56   64   50</p>
<p> 15.Sporting Gijon	  42  13  11  18  45   63   50</p>
<p> 16.Celta Vigo		42  12  13  17  51   54   49</p>
<p> 17.Oviedo		    42  12  12  18  48   64   48</p>
<p> 18.Rayo Vallecano	  42  13   6  23  43   62   45</p>
<p> 19.Extremadura	     42  11  11  20  35   64   44</p>
<p> 20.Sevilla		   42  12   7  23  50   69   43</p>
<p> 21.Hercules		  42  12   5  25  40   76   41</p>
<p> 22.Logrones		  42   9   6  27  33   85   33</p>
<p>Note: Final standings of teams level on points are decided</p>
<p>by net results of the two games between them.</p>
<p>Real Madrid and Barcelona have qualified for the European</p>
<p>Cup. Deportivo Coruna, Atletico Madrid, Athletic Bilbao and</p>
<p>Valladolid have qualifed for the UEFA Cup. Real Betis will play</p>
<p>the Cup Winners' Cup.</p>
<p>Relegated directly: Logrones, Sevilla, Hercules and</p>
<p>Extremadura.</p>
<p>Merida and Salamanca are promoted from the second division</p>
<p>(only two teams are promoted as the first division will be</p>
<p>reduced in size from 22 to 20 teams next season).</p>
<p>Rayo Vallecano will play off for the last place with</p>
<p>Mallorca of the second division.</p>
